nd of arthur and his sword  excalibur so it's not about strength  it's about  having the soul of a selfless hero to be  worthy to lift the weapon  and it's not that cap's recent heroics  in infinity war in an end game made him  suddenly worthy to pull this sword from  the stone he was always able to do it  arguably born able to do it that's why  he was chosen for the super soldier  experiment in the 40s dr erskine and  peggy carter saw that  even as a scrawny guy he possessed a  selflessness  and perseverance that when coupled with  physical strength would make him  unstoppable  really cap lifting mjolnir was a payoff  to the moment in the first avengers  movie  the argument between stark and cap when  cap accused tony of being  selfish and arrogant and tony accused  cap of just being a fortunate lab  experiment as opposed to being a hero  who  had to build himself the way tony did  everything special about you came out of  a bottle  endgame proved wrong both cap and stark  from that argument stark made the  sacrifice play in this movie and kat  proved that there was always a greater  worthiness to him than his super  strength and super agility  that was just stuff that did come out of  a bottle but the truly worthy soul  came from the fighter who could do this  all day i'm curious to know how all of  you guys reacted to this moment where  mjolnir was lifted so comment down below  with your best reaction  and follow me on instagram and twitter  at yavos subscribe to new rockstars and  subscribe to our inside marvel podcast  feed for early access to all of our  marvel coverage thank you for joining me  and um  when i needed my uber driver to lift my  heavy luggage into the trunk  uh yeah that was just me being like  happened acting polite to make him feel  better about his strength i was totally  worthy  [Music]  you
 

